FEX: honour a free mmap hint below 4 GiB in the 64-bit low window (SteamARM, Darwin host)

Linux places a non-fixed mapping at its hint when the range is free. Darwin
maps nothing below 4 GiB, so in the 64-bit low window (fex-lxrt-guest-base.patch,
FEX_LOWWINDOW=1) such a hint went to the host and landed above 4 GiB. x86-64
ART reserves its boot image at ART_BASE_ADDRESS (0x70000000) plus a random
delta that way, got another address back, and ran without a boot image
("Failed to mmap at expected address, mapped at 0x10e4e8000 instead of
0x6f7a0000", MEASURED, benchmarks/stage25-art-x86-fex.txt). The window's
allocator now tries the hint as MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE first; a taken range
falls back to the previous behaviour. 64-bit guests with a guest base only;
32-bit guests and 64-bit processes without the window are unchanged.

diff --git a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SyscallsSMCTracking.cpp b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SyscallsSMCTracking.cpp
--- a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SyscallsSMCTracking.cpp
+++ b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SyscallsSMCTracking.cpp
@@ -373,7 +373,23 @@
         reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(addr) + length <= (1ULL << 32)) {
       Map32Bit = true;
     }
-    if (Map32Bit) {
+    // A plain hint below 4 GiB (no MAP_FIXED) in the 64-bit low window: Linux
+    // places the mapping there when the range is free, and only elsewhere
+    // when it is not. The host (Darwin) never can, so the window's allocator
+    // tries the hint as MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE; if that range is taken the
+    // mapping goes where it would have gone before. x86-64 ART reserves its
+    // boot image this way, at 0x70000000 plus a random delta, and fell back
+    // to running without it ("Failed to mmap at expected address", MEASURED,
+    // SteamARM benchmarks/stage25-art-x86-fex.txt).
+    bool HintDone = false;
+    if (!Map32Bit && Is64Bit && FEX::HLE::GuestBase && addr && !(flags & (MAP_FIXED | FEX_MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE)) &&
+        reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(addr) < (1ULL << 32) && length <= (1ULL << 32) - reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(addr)) {
+      Result = (uint64_t)Get32BitAllocator()->Mmap((void*)addr, length, prot, flags | FEX_MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE, fd, offset);
+      HintDone = !FEX::HLE::HasSyscallError(Result);
+    }
+    if (HintDone) {
+      // Placed at the hint, inside the window.
+    } else if (Map32Bit) {
       Result = (uint64_t)Get32BitAllocator()->Mmap((void*)addr, length, prot, flags, fd, offset);
       if (FEX::HLE::HasSyscallError(Result)) {
         return reinterpret_cast<void*>(Result);
